# DogeOS RPC package settings for mainnet.
#
# Mainnet is not released yet; see README.md in this directory.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory, fill in the required values, and keep it
# private:
#   cd mainnet && cp env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
# Docker Compose and the scripts in this directory read .env automatically.
# This is the only file you edit; everything else here is maintained by the
# package.

# L1 Interface paths inside /data are fixed by the package. Change DATA_ROOT
# to select the host disk; do not override individual database/artifact paths.

# --- Required ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path on this host's data disk for Dogecoin, L2Reth, and L1 Interface
# data and snapshot downloads. Not inside this repository. Check that the disk
# is mounted (for example: findmnt -T /data).
DATA_ROOT=/path/to/dogeos-data/mainnet

# Dogecoin RPC credentials, passed to dogecoin-node and l1-interface as Docker
# secrets. Set a strong password; Dogecoin refuses to start while it is empty.
# Letters, digits, and ._~:@%+=,- only. Keep them stable afterwards.
DOGECOIN_RPC_USER=doge
DOGECOIN_RPC_PASSWORD=

# --- Persistent L2 P2P identity and operator allowlists ----------------------

# Run python3 scripts/p2p-identity.py init BEFORE restoring or starting.
# Default private key: ${DATA_ROOT}/l2reth-identity/discovery-secret.
# Optional absolute path outside chain data and this repository; never put the
# private key itself in .env. Keep the key and its backup private (mode 600).
# L2RETH_P2P_KEY_FILE=/your/private/identity/discovery-secret
# Reachable static IPv4 advertised to peers; forwards L2_P2P_PORT TCP and UDP.
# L2RETH_P2P_PUBLIC_IP=203.0.113.10
# Actual outbound public source CIDRs for the operations team, comma-separated.
# Behind NAT these may differ from the advertised IP. Report only, not a local
# firewall rule. Replace documentation addresses with your real configuration.
# L2RETH_P2P_SOURCE_CIDRS=203.0.113.10/32
# Run python3 scripts/p2p-identity.py show; send its PUBLIC output to operations
# and wait for IP/public-key allowlisting. See docs/p2p-identity.md.

# --- Optional (defaults shown) -----------------------------------------------

# Host ports.
# DOGECOIN_RPC_PORT=22555
# L2_HTTP_PORT=8545
# L2_WS_PORT=8546
# L2_P2P_PORT=30303
# L2_METRICS_PORT=6060        # Prometheus, always on 127.0.0.1

# Interface for the Dogecoin RPC and L1 Interface ports (8547, 5052, 9090).
# INTERNAL_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1

# Ethereum execution RPC used by L1 Interface.
# DOGEOS_ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=

# Temporary use of an external Dogecoin RPC instead of the bundled node (see
# docs/operations.md in this directory before switching).
# DOGEOS_EXTERNAL_DOGECOIN_RPC_URL=https://your-dogecoin-rpc
# DOGEOS_EXTERNAL_DOGECOIN_RPC_USER=
# DOGEOS_EXTERNAL_DOGECOIN_RPC_PASSWORD=

# L2Reth RPC. debug and trace are on; filter and rate-limit them in your
# gateway. Extra rollup-node flags are separated by spaces and must not repeat
# flags the package already sets (for example --rpc.max-connections).
# L2RETH_HTTP_API=eth,net,web3,debug,trace
# L2RETH_WS_API=eth,net,web3,debug,trace
# L2RETH_EXTRA_ARGS=--rpc.max-tracing-requests 8

# Memory and log rotation. Dogecoin uses about 3 GB on mainnet; the limit
# leaves room for startup and chain growth.
# DOGECOIN_MEM_RESERVATION=4g
# DOGECOIN_MEM_LIMIT=8g
# L2Reth defaults to 16 GB. Set this to suit your machine and RPC workload,
# leaving memory for Dogecoin, L1 Interface, the OS, and other services.
# L2RETH_MEM_LIMIT=16g
# L1_INTERFACE_MEM_LIMIT=2g
# LOG_MAX_SIZE=100m
# LOG_MAX_FILE=5
